ible. Hmm.\n\nThe proposal says without native logging cannot legally operate, so existential gate. Implementing a logging SDK across all deployments is substantial engineering effort. I'd say 2 (significant change, expensive/difficult). Maybe 3. Let's pick 3? The anchored: 4 easy low cost or non-radical changes. 3 some changes, or reasonably feasible measures. 2 significant change, or expensive or difficult, but not totally impossible. Retrofitting existing pipelines is significant. I'd go with 2.\n\nAcceptability (1-4): common strategies that violate no norms =4. Logging is legally required, acceptable. So 4.\n\nEffectiveness (1-4): degree will solve problem. Reasonable and will solve stated problem without regard for workability ->4. It directly addresses logging mandate. Yes will solve main problem. So 4.\n\nApplicability (1-4): solves identified problem directly related to stated problem ->4. Do X to get Y, Y is part of stated problem. Yes.\n\nNeed one sentence evidence for each rating.\n\nProvide output echoing id exactly.\n\nFormat: probably JSON or list. Instructions: For each subscale give \"<subscale>_evidence\" first then \"<subscale>\" integer. Likely produce lines.\n\nWill output:\n\nid: P1694\nparadigm_relatedness_evidence: ...\nparadigm_relatedness: 2\n...\n\nMake sure one sentence evidence.\n\nLet's craft sentences.\n\nparadigm_relatedness_evidence: The proposal adds a logging SDK and retrofit process but keeps R&D and compliance separate, treating compliance as standard logging practice rather than changing the lab’s research-compliance relationship. Score 2.\n\noriginality_evidence: Embedding tamper-evident event logging to meet Article 12 is a common, routine compliance engineering response expected from AI labs. Score 1.\n\nimplementability_evidence: Designing a platform-wide SDK and retrofitting existing high-risk pipelines before next release requires significant engineering resources and pipeline changes. Score 2.\n\nacceptability_evidence: Automated logging for traceability is legally mandated and socially expected, violating no norms or sensibilities. Score 4.\n\neffectiveness_evidence: Native tamper-evident logging of Article 12(2) events and Annex III 1(a) minimums directly provides the legally required capability to operate in the EU. Score 4.\n\napplicability_evidence: The proposal directly addresses how the lab must meet the Article 12 logging mandate for high-risk AI systems. Score 4.\n\nReturn.\n\n",
