l directly implements automatic event recording required by Article 12(1)-(3) for high-risk prototypes, which is the stated compliance problem. => applicability 4\n\nEffectiveness evidence: If implemented, the SDK would capture usage periods, reference databases, matched inputs and verifier identities as mandated, thereby solving the logging mandate. => effectiveness 4\n\nOriginality evidence: Embedding a reusable logging SDK with compliance sign-off is a common, mundane engineering practice for regulated systems. => originality 1\n\nParadigm_relatedness evidence: It introduces new tooling and a compliance gate but still treats compliance as logging practice without changing the lab's R&D paradigm. => paradigm_relatedness 2\n\nImplementability evidence: Building an open-source SDK with pluggable adapters and version control requires platform engineering effort but is reasonably feasible for an R&D lab. => implementability 3\n\nAcceptability evidence: Mandating logs and compliance sign-off aligns with legal requirements and offends no norms or sensibilities. => acceptability 4\n\nReturn.\n\n",
