ing echoing id. Provide lines.\n\nI'll output:\nid: P1631\nacceptability_evidence: ...\nacceptability: 4\n...\n\nMake sure one sentence evidence.\n\nLet's craft concise sentences.\n\nAcceptability evidence: The proposal uses mandated logs for research and open publication, which aligns with regulatory transparency goals and does not violate legal or ethical norms. Score 4.\n\nImplementability evidence: Building six-month rolling log pipelines and validating detection algorithms requires new engineering and methodology work but is feasible within an R&D lab. Score 3.\n\nOriginality evidence: Reframing compulsory compliance logs as a longitudinal scientific dataset for drift detection is unusual and shows imagination beyond routine logging. Score 3.\n\nParadigm_relatedness evidence: It weaves logging into core scientific work and creates new research outputs from compliance data, changing how R&D relates to regulatory obligations. Score 3.\n\nApplicability evidence: The project directly addresses the mandate to technically allow automatic recording of events and to enable traceability and post-market monitoring. Score 4.\n\nEffectiveness evidence: If implemented it would satisfy logging requirements and generate useful monitoring tools, though it does not by itself guarantee full Annex III point-specific record keeping for all high-risk systems. Score 3.\n\nReturn.\n\n",
