le>\". Might be just lines.\n\nProbably output JSON with id and fields.\n\nProvide one sentence evidence for each rating.\n\nLet's craft concise sentences.\n\nacceptability_evidence: Centralized logging is a standard engineering practice that complies with Article 12 without raising legal, privacy, or political concerns. => acceptability 4\n\nimplementability_evidence: Deploying a shared service on existing servers with a four-person pod for two quarters and three pilot retrofits is a reasonably feasible organizational change. => implementability 3\n\neffectiveness_evidence: Standardizing schema across projects would provide automatic event logs covering Article 12(1)-(3) requirements, solving the traceability mandate. => effectiveness 4\n\napplicability_evidence: The proposal directly addresses how to meet the logging mandate and preserve R&D hours for the regulated lab. => applicability 4\n\nparadigm_relatedness_evidence: It introduces a shared tool and schema but still treats compliance as a logging practice rather than changing the lab's R&D-compliance relationship. => paradigm_relatedness 2\n\noriginality_evidence: Shared centralized logging for regulatory compliance is a common, mundane software engineering approach. => originality 1\n\nProvide output.\n\n",
