t ingenious... Proposal is embed auto-logging into pipelines, retrofit with modules. This is common? For AI labs, implementing logging for compliance is fairly standard. Originality likely 1 = common, mundane, boring. Might be 2 = interesting? Probably common. I'd say 1.\n\nParadigm_relatedness: degree to which idea preserves or modifies paradigm. Proposal treats compliance as logging practice, introduces new elements tools formats processes but still treats compliance as logging practice. That is slightly paradigm stretching: introduces new elements (tools, formats, processes) but still treats compliance as logging practice => level 2.\n\nAcceptability: socially legally politically acceptable. Common strategies that violate no norms. Engineering integration, tamper-evident logs. Acceptable. Level 4.\n\nImplementability: degree to which can be easily implemented. Small cross-team task force of four engineers spends one quarter wrapping current orchestration tools... some changes or reasonably feasible measures => level 3? Could be easy to implement at low cost? Four engineers one quarter is moderate cost. Might be 3 = some changes, or reasonably feasible measures. Or 4 = easy to implement at low cost, or non-radical changes. Wrapping MLflow/Kubeflow with hooks might be non-trivial. I'd say 3.\n\nLet's output format: echo id, then for each subscale evidence sentence then score.\n\nNeed \"<subscale>_evidence\" first then \"<subscale>\". Probably lines.\n\nReturn rating of proposal, echoing its id exactly. For each subscale... give \"<subscale>_evidence\" (one sentence) first and then \"<subscale>\" (an integer level).\n\nProvide JSON? Probably just plain text. Safer to output structured.\n\nI'll produce:\n\nid: P2832\neffectiveness_evidence: ...\neffectiveness: 4\n...\n\nEnsure one sentence evidence.\n\nLet's craft sentences.\n\neffectiveness_evidence: The proposal directly builds automatic event capture, risk flagging and tamper-evident storage mapped to Article 12(2