ting? I think common.\n\nSo ratings:\nimplementability evidence sentence then score.\nacceptability ...\napplicability...\neffectiveness...\nparadigm_relatedness...\noriginality...\n\nNeed format: For each subscale give \"<subscale>_evidence\" (one sentence) first and then \"<subscale>\" (integer). Probably each on separate line.\n\nReturn rating echoing id exactly.\n\nLet's produce:\n\nP2726\nimplementability_evidence: ...\nimplementability: 4? Let's choose 3 to be safe. The description says easy to implement at low cost, or non-radical changes. Amending internal grant allocation rule requires committee approval and process change - maybe some changes. I'll give 3.\n\nacceptability_evidence: ... acceptability:4\n\napplicability_evidence: ... applicability:3? Might be 4. Let's pick 3 = solves implied problem related. Actually budgeting is directly enabling logging mandate compliance. Hmm.\n\nThe stated problem: decide how to respond: how to meet logging mandate and/or adapt R&D accordingly. Embedding costs is adapting R&D resource planning. That's direct adaptation. Could be 4.\n\nLet's choose applicability 4.\n\neffectiveness 3\n\nparadigm_relatedness 2\n\noriginality 1\n\nProvide one sentence evidence each.\n\nEnsure one sentence per evidence.\n\nLet's output JSON? Probably simple list.\n\nWill return:\n\nid: P2726\nimplementability_evidence: ...\nimplementability: 3\n...\n\nLet's do that.\n\n",
